WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Stress is force per area. Strain is a change

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.320
in shape or volume. With elastic strain, removing the

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.000
load restores the sample. Permanent deformation occurs by fracture

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.760
or ductile change. On the course graph, depth increases

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.520
downward and strength increases rightward. In the brittle upper

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.660
crust, increasing confinement makes fractures harder to develop. The

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.700
curve approaches a maximum. Deeper, higher temperature promotes solid-state

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.560
ductile flow. Watch the solid rock bend. The curve

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:33.380
turns toward lower strength. The brittle–ductile transition is gradual;

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.700
its depth depends on conditions, not one universal number.
